<title>USA: Caterpillar to spend $36 mln on renovations.</title>
<headline>Caterpillar to spend $36 mln on renovations.</headline>
<dateline>PEORIA, Ill. 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caterpillar Inc said Tuesday it would invest $36 million to renovate three facilites in Peoria to support growth.</p>
<p>The company said it has hired 1,200 new workers since the beginning of last year, and it needed space to accommodate them.  </p>
<p>Caterpillar said it planned to renovate three facilities in and near Peoria and relocate and centralize employees to improve efficiencies. No employees will lose their jobs as a result of the changes, which do not involve any of the company's manufacturing plants.</p>
<p>The company said it expected to create an additional 360,000 square feet of office and product training lab space.</p>
<p>-- ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
